{"availability":"available","full":"murtuzabuilds/outpost","name":"outpost","description":"A base of operations for AI agents: see the crew, set what each bot may touch, and decide the risky calls yourself. A 3D concept build.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T17:39:01Z","updated":"2026-10-14T05:59:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://murtuzabuilds.github.io/outpost/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T07:19:47.652Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T07:19:47.652Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T07:19:47.652Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.665Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-13T07:35:50.376Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T07:19:47.652Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The control room for the person who runs a company's AI agents.","Interactive demo · sample data · Case study · Umbra · Portfolio","Outpost is a concept product I designed and built. It is the control room for the person who runs a company's approved AI agents day to day. Each bot acts alone up to a limit it has earned, and anything risky waits at the Gate for a person's yes. It shows who on the crew is working and who is waiting, keeps a record of every decision, and lets you test a change to those limits on replayed shifts before it is applied."],"features":["They cannot see who needs them. In a table of logs a blocked agent looks the same as a busy one, and a blocked agent produces nothing.","Agents have no limits of authority. People do. A new hire cannot sign a $5,000 refund. In a 2026 Cloud Security Alliance survey, 53% of organisations said their agents had gone beyond their intended permissions (CSA,…","Approving everything does not scale. With enough agents, the person stops reading and starts clicking.","Nobody knows what a rule change will do until it is applied.","Kestrel Mutual is fictional."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/murtuzabuilds/outpost/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"05d05e8c18b543c7257becf94f32077433ddfce1de81fd03dc97a23045402d4f","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.761Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.761Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The control room for the person who runs a company's AI agents.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/murtuzabuilds/outpost/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"05d05e8c18b543c7257becf94f32077433ddfce1de81fd03dc97a23045402d4f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/murtuzabuilds/outpost/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.762Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T22:04:48Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/murtuzabuilds/outpost/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.762Z","hash":"05d05e8c18b543c7257becf94f32077433ddfce1de81fd03dc97a23045402d4f","originalBytes":13707,"storedBytes":13707,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.665Z","subjects":["MCP servers & agents","3D & graphics"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"AI & machine learning","subjects":["MCP servers & agents","3D & graphics"],"evidence":[{"subject":"MCP servers & agents","source":"metadata","match":"AI agents"},{"subject":"3D & graphics","source":"metadata","match":"3D"}],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Simulation & physics","Automation & workflows","Portfolios & personal sites"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://murtuzabuilds.github.io/outpost/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-14T14:47:42.969Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-14T14:47:42.969Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-14T14:47:42.969Z","target":"https://murtuzabuilds.com/outpost/","failureCount":0,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-21T14:47:42.969Z"},"previewAt